Designed with open green spaces, a civic square, community building, creche and local retail space.

The neighbourhood borders large parkland, giving residents plenty of outdoor space.

The standout local feature is Corkagh Park one of Dublin’s biggest public parks with:

Walking and cycling paths

Playgrounds

Sports facilities like baseball and cricket grounds

Allotments and natural areas

Nearby, you’re also close to traditional Dublin heritage spots such as the Clondalkin Round Tower (in neighbouring Clondalkin).

Kilcarbery Grange benefits from good connections:

Easy road access via the Outer Ring Road (R136) linking quickly to the M7, M4 and M50.

Bus routes serving Dublin city and suburbs.

Close enough (by bike/car) to train stations at Clondalkin/Fonthill, Adamstown and soon Kishoge.

